WEBVTT

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:10.320
Howdy! Mosey on in to Fleur de Lapin!

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.990
Your greeting is all wrong!

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.460
And quit flaunting your chest so excessively!

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:16.450
Why is that a problem...?

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:17.950
Sheesh!

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:21.420
Are you really here to work part time
because you're short on money?

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.830
I'm just copying you, Syaro!
Earning extra by working multiple jobs!

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:27.380
This is what you get for buying 
a bunch of stuff at that

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:29.690
flea market, like doorknobs 
and Chino's magic set.

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:32.130
As if you have any room to talk.

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:33.630
You bought that tea set and stuff.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.790
The two of us~!

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:41.670
Our wallets may be empty, 
but our hearts are full~!

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:43.710
And so are our chests~!

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.290
Stop singing, stop dancing,
and stop lumping me with you!

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:48.210
My chest is not full!

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:49.980
Yay!

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:57.040
Bunnisode 10:
A Request for Backup From a Full Heart

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:02.130
Spin around with a twirl, hey, dance dance

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:05.210
In the heavenly cafeteria, dance dance

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.750
Where is the door? (Over here!)

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:11.250
Take a hop into the cup (Leap right in!)

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:14.830
Big puffy clouds float through the sky

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:17.960
They actually taste sweet, 
for real (Just kidding!)

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:21.000
If we fly through the sky 
in tea cups and coffee cups

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.000
We can go anywhere together

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:30.710
Wanting to be a dreamer forever 
(More impossible than possible)

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:36.380
Think about how exciting tomorrow 
will be (So many flavors to try!)

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:38.960
Cinnamon instead of sugar

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:43.000
If that becomes a preference, 
it might be time for evolution

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.290
Going to a new place (Were you invited?)

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:49.040
If you get invited there, 
let's take the plunge and fly

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:52.210
(C'mon ride in the tea cup 
and soar through the sky)

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:54.500
(C'mon ride in the coffee cup, yeah yeah)

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:58.330
Spin around with a twirl, hey, 
dance dance (Dance dance!)

00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:01.540
In the heavenly cafeteria, 
dance dance (Dance dance)

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:05.040
Where is the door? It's inside of the cup

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:07.580
An illusion? Or reality? Which?

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:10.790
It doesn't really matter 
either way (Good point)

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:14.040
A dollop of whip cream on 
your head (Fluff fluff)

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:20.000
Okay, just dance (The future) it'll 
definitely be fun (So let's fly!)

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:23.500
Flying through the sky in 
tea cups and coffee cups

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:26.290
We can go anywhere together!

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:31.380
What are you doing?

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.580
The final line of defense...

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:39.830
It's time to break open 
my beloved Kigumin bank.

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:43.260
It's the type you have to smash?
Why'd you bring it here?!

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:47.880
Kigumin! Say your prayers!

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:49.810
Take this!

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:52.040
Kigumin...!

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:56.210
O-only 52 yen?!

00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:59.900
No way... I thought there 
was at least 5,000 in there.

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:02.380
S-Syaro...?

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.630
I've got 10 more yen than you do!

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:12.290
This is not the sort of 
thing I wanna compete over!

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:18.300
Rize has worked here part-time 
before too, right?

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:21.630
Welcome!

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:26.040
That's right. She had a sudden 
need for cash back then.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:27.680
Yeah, and now so do I!

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:29.580
Is there something you're desperate to buy?

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:34.440
I dunno if I should share. 
Maybe I'll keep it a secret...

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.590
Quit playing coy with me!

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:37.420
Well, actually...

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:39.130
Good day!

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:42.920
I came to relax and recharge.

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:47.080
I promise not to do any inappropriate peeking,
so please don't chase me out.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:49.170
Howdy there, Miss Aoyama!

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:50.330
Why are you armed?!

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:52.000
Put that hammer down already!

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:56.460
Order up, one cup of chamomile!

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:59.880
It's hot outta the pot! Drink 
up before it cools down!

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:02.790
Wow, it's so fragrant.

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:07.380
This is very relaxing.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.710
Herbal teas really are quite incredible.

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:11.770
I know, right?

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:14.380
Suppose I'll sit down and join you for some!

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:17.290
This feels kind of weird.

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:17.710
Please do your job.

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:21.380
I never thought I would be
working together with Cocoa at Fleur.

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:21.380
Please do your job.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:26.630
B-but it's not like I'm enjoying it at all!

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:33.920
My next job is at the crepe shop.

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:40.800
Welcome in! I'm Cocoa, I just started here!

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:42.080
She's here, too!

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:49.380
You really are amazing,
working so many jobs all the time.

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:51.790
A-anybody can do it once they get used to it!

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:55.500
Jeez, you've got it all over your face.

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:57.670
Thanks.

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:00.170
This is so hard to do!

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:04.880
Syaro, how many days will it 
take until I get good at this?!

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:04.880
You know... work's not so bad like this.

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:13.500
Next up, my job at the bookstore.

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:24.960
I'm not even the slightest bit sad at the idea
that Cocoa won't be there!

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:27.340
Author Aoyama Blue Mountain
Book Signing Event
END OF THE LINE

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:30.070
Oh! We're seeing a lot of each other today!

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:31.600
HERE, TOO?!

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:39.000
Excuse me, Rize, we haven't 
gotten any orders for toast...

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.860
Huh?! Oh, right!

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:45.750
Seeing Cocoa's bread brings back memories
of when things used to be more lively in here.

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:48.160
She's just working a few 
other jobs to earn money.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:51.750
I know that! But you're 
just as guilty, Chino.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:52.620
Huh?

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.830
Are all of those filled with Kilimanjaro?

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:57.610
M-my attention was so focused on worrying about Cocoa

00:05:57.610 --> 00:05:59.860
causing problems for Syaro that it just happened...

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:01.630
How absent-minded can you two get?

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:04.510
Who's going to eat all that?

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:08.830
I worry about our cafe's future...

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:14.350
We deeply appreciate your willingness

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:18.090
to wear costumes
from Miss Aoyama's novels just for today's signing event!

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:22.330
Of course, but what novel 
did your costumes come from?

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:25.030
"The Barista That Became a Rabbit"!

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:27.330
Hoppity, hoppity, hop!

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:29.530
All I see is an adult who's goofing around!

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:33.170
But, you know, Miss Aoyama 
sure has amusing ideas!

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:35.830
You're such a kind editor to go along
with her crazy whims like this.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:38.750
M-m-m-m-my apologies!

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:40.710
So the costumes were actually your idea!

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:48.920
Author Aoyama Blue Mountain
Book Signing Event
END OF THE LINE

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:51.880
Miss Aoyama Blue Mountain's
book signing event will begin shortly!

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:56.130
Anyone with a numbered ticket
please line up in front of the store!

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:05.190
I hope my present fund gets filled up fast!

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:06.810
"Present fund"?

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:08.790
Yeah! For Christmas!

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:11.330
Is that why you're doing all these jobs?

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:12.770
That's right!

00:07:12.770 --> 00:07:15.080
Look forward to getting 
something nice, Syaro!

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:16.170
No way!

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:19.710
You're working so hard for the money,
you should use it on yourself instead!

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:21.380
That's what I'm doing!

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:22.540
Huh?

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:25.740
I'm buying presents to give 
because it's fun for me.

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:28.420
I love taking the time to 
pick out the perfect one!

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:32.170
For example...

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:36.100
I'm picturing myself
buying king melon bread to give to you!

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:39.130
King melon bread...

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:42.330
Yes! That's the expression I love to see!

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:43.920
King melon bread...

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:46.580
Hooray!

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:49.830
And for Rize...

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:56.740
"The Bunny who Bounds Across 
the Battlefield," maybe?

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:56.740
The Bunny who Bounds Across the Battlefield
Ep 1: The Mercenary Known as Bunny

00:07:56.740 --> 00:08:00.880
Not that one! Senpai would definitely prefer
"The Rabbit Master of Disguise"!

00:07:58.630 --> 00:08:03.370
The Rabbit Master of Disguise

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:03.040
I know that she'd love it!

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:05.880
I can't wait to see Senpai's smiling face...

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:12.290
The two of us~

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:15.000
Our wallets may be empty...

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.470
but our hearts are full~!

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:18.390
And so are our chests~!

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:20.830
No mine's not~!

00:08:21.170 --> 00:08:23.140
Is that song some kind of new fad?

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:24.900
Senpai?!

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:26.960
We're here, too!

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:27.830
Hello!

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:31.050
So this is where you were 
working today, Cocoa.

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:32.790
The Chimame Corps is on the scene!

00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:33.900
We are!

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:36.250
What about Rabbit House?

00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:39.030
Did you close it up for today
because nobody was coming?

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:41.510
How rude! We had plenty of customers!

00:08:41.510 --> 00:08:44.920
My father told us to go have fun
and leave everything to him.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:47.210
We didn't want to miss the book signing!

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:54.050
Wow, you all came to see me.

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:57.080
Miss Aoyama! Congrats on 
your book signing event!

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:58.170
Congrats!

00:08:58.170 --> 00:08:59.540
Congratulations.

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:01.560
Such beautiful flowers.

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:02.950
We have some for Miss Rin, too.

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:04.330
Huh? For me?

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:06.170
And a little gift.

00:09:06.170 --> 00:09:07.170
Me?!

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:08.080
Oh my!

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:11.750
Thank you so much, everyone.

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:15.460
Chiya?

00:09:15.460 --> 00:09:17.320
I'm glad that I made it in time!

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:20.170
I'm here to celebrate with Miss Aoyama, too!

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:22.420
Just check out this picture!

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:24.710
Good job!

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:25.960
Good job!

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:27.210
Gimme that!

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:33.250
U-uh, we didn't prepare anything for you...

00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:35.540
Our wallets and chests are so dismal...

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:37.840
Your chest is definitely NOT dismal!

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:39.860
So heartwarming.
Why are you so mad?!

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:41.960
So heartwarming.

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:48.920
Today was such a wonderful day!
Thank you so, so much!

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:50.980
The signing hasn't even started yet!

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:55.630
It seems like we've gotten our Christmas presents
from you just a little early.

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:58.360
Christmas present?

00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:01.290
Hey! Are you guys gonna have
another Christmas party this year?

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:03.880
I want to do a gift exchange!

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:06.760
Just let your big sister handle everything!

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:07.750
Yay!

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:10.280
You're going to go broke again!

00:10:10.280 --> 00:10:12.840
A gift exchange? That sounds great!

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:17.420
But picking a gift that could work
for anybody is pretty difficult.

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:18.510
That's true.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:22.010
In that case, why not make 
it a Secret Santa event?

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:24.790
Secret Santa?

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:31.210
Is everyone ready?

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:36.130
We just have to prepare a gift
for the person whose name we draw, right?

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:37.290
Right.

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:39.130
Here we go!

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:41.670
Secret Santa!

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:46.250
Say, whose name did- wait, I shouldn't ask!

00:10:47.420 --> 00:10:48.790
It's hard not to let it slip.

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:52.510
But we're not supposed to know
who our Santa is until Christmas.

00:10:52.510 --> 00:10:53.920
I'm so looking forward to it!

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:56.170
Wham!

00:10:56.540 --> 00:10:58.330
I'm curious who you ended up with!

00:10:58.330 --> 00:11:00.330
Let me see!

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:03.040
Oh, please. Showing you 
would ruin all the fun!

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:05.380
That was amazing, Syaro! You move like a pro!

00:11:06.630 --> 00:11:08.040
You handled that well.

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:10.290
It's going to be a challenge 
to keep this a secret.

00:11:10.630 --> 00:11:13.170
Whoa! You look like you're 
itching with excitement!

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:17.580
It feels strange that we're all keeping secrets
from each other like this...

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:21.830
But a party with a Secret Santa,
there's so much to look forward to.

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:23.630
That's true.

00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:26.250
And a certain someone was telling 
me earlier how they loved

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:28.010
"taking the time to pick out" gifts.

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:28.830
Cocoa

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:36.840
I guess... she's going to need 
a new bank to save up in.

00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:43.830
I see some resemblance.

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:46.540
So, are you the one who pulled Cocoa's name
for Secret Santa?

00:11:46.540 --> 00:11:48.080
N-n-n-n-no I didn't!

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:50.500
What are you looking at over there, Syaro?

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:54.000
DON'T COME OVER HERE!

00:11:55.500 --> 00:12:02.740
Author Aoyama Blue Mountain
Book Signing

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:58.210
I can't wait to read your next book!

00:11:58.210 --> 00:11:59.750
Thank you.

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:02.750
We hope for your continued support!

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:04.790
Chino...!

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:18.710
Everywhere you look it's dazzling.

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:23.410
Yeah, the Christmas season is the 
busiest time of year for most stores.

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:25.090
They really go all out for it!

00:12:25.750 --> 00:12:30.630
But it seems like things are going to be
pretty quiet at our cafe this year.

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:32.560
Since both Cocoa and Rize are...

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:35.770
My Santa is proving to be 
extra popular this year.

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:38.780
All the customers and 
their kids are so excited!

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:41.070
So they asked if I could keep working there
just a while longer.

00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:44.330
A member of the theater club was 
injured and they asked me to

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:46.070
fill in for next week's performance...

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:49.670
I'm sorry, Chino! I promise 
I'll make it up to you!

00:12:49.670 --> 00:12:51.670
I hate to do it, but please 
let me take a break from work!

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:56.080
W-well, I'm totally fine 
managing the cafe by myself.

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:57.660
You're whole body is shaking.

00:12:57.660 --> 00:12:59.280
Because I'm cold!

00:12:59.280 --> 00:13:01.080
Guess whooooo~!

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:03.290
Th-this voice has to be Cocoa!

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:05.720
Jeez, what are you doing 
when you should be wor-?

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:07.540
Wait, that voice was Syaro's?!

00:13:08.460 --> 00:13:10.040
Did I sound like Cocoa?

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:14.710
Y-yes. You totally nailed the "openly selfish
and stupid" tone that she always has.

00:13:14.710 --> 00:13:15.750
Oh really?

00:13:16.210 --> 00:13:17.250
Guess who!

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:19.750
This chivalrous voice must belong to Senpai!

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:22.290
You can try to disguise your 
voice, but I'll always know!

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:24.210
Boo!

00:13:26.170 --> 00:13:28.780
Y-YOU DIDN'T SOUND LIKE SENPAI AT ALL!

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:30.290
But I fooled you!

00:13:30.290 --> 00:13:31.670
No, you did not!

00:13:31.670 --> 00:13:34.290
They've got so much energy despite the cold.

00:13:31.670 --> 00:13:34.290
Uh-huh, that's just what you 
want everyone to believe.

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:40.540
Heading to meet Cocoa 
after her part-time job?

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:43.890
Uh, yes. It looked like it might rain,
so I brought her an umbrella.

00:13:43.890 --> 00:13:47.430
Chino, is it true you're going to work
the cafe all by yourself?

00:13:47.750 --> 00:13:49.170
So you overheard that...

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:50.960
Are you going to be okay?

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:53.630
M-my father will be with 
me, so it's not a problem.

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:56.000
Shouldering too much on your own
is bad for your health!

00:13:56.670 --> 00:14:00.310
Rize scolded me about that back
when I was working during Halloween.

00:14:01.210 --> 00:14:04.040
I bet if Senpai were here,
she'd put it something like this...

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:08.130
"When the chips are down,
never hesitate to put in a request for backup!"

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:10.790
Wow!

00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:17.210
Those two were really enjoying themselves.

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:22.200
I guess this market has an atmosphere
that just makes people excited.

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:26.470
Buy some, buy some! Pretty please!

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:26.470
This voice...

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:29.630
If you don't buy some,
I'll go around calling you "Big Sis" all day!

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:29.630
Pleaaaaaaaaaaaaase!

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:30.330
Cut it out, you two!

00:14:30.330 --> 00:14:32.540
Buy some, buy some!

00:14:30.330 --> 00:14:32.570
I'm gonna start calling you "Sensei"!

00:14:32.570 --> 00:14:33.380
Stop!

00:14:32.630 --> 00:14:36.480
C'mon, c'mon!

00:14:34.330 --> 00:14:36.670
Hello, Rize, Maya and Megu.

00:14:36.670 --> 00:14:38.250
Oh, it's Chino!

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:39.500
Hi, Chino!

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:44.340
Please help! These two are 
pestering me to no end!

00:14:44.340 --> 00:14:46.040
You seem happy about it...

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:48.580
Come on! Join us, Chino!

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:50.170
Uh, right.

00:14:52.420 --> 00:14:56.880
Please... please buy us some.

00:14:57.920 --> 00:14:59.790
Pretty please!

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:01.790
Buy us some! Please!

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:02.250
C'mon!

00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:05.080
All right. I give up already.

00:15:08.330 --> 00:15:09.630
So yummy!

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:11.390
You better keep up your studies.

00:15:11.390 --> 00:15:13.960
Of course! We'll totally study!

00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:17.420
I'm gonna become a high 
schooler just like Rize!

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:21.210
Good idea. Rize's such a 
reliable person, after all.

00:15:23.170 --> 00:15:25.900
M-my wallet... I left it at home!

00:15:26.130 --> 00:15:29.160
So much for that "reliable" 
comment I just made.

00:15:29.160 --> 00:15:31.380
Yeesh, the things I put up with.

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:33.140
Maya...!

00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:36.670
It's okay for you to rely on 
me once in a while, you know?

00:15:36.670 --> 00:15:38.710
Says the girl shaking me down for treats!

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:45.170
Those three were enjoying themselves, too.

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:47.080
The excitement of the market strikes again.

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:50.380
Indeed. And it's affected you, too.

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:53.290
This way!

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:55.290
Stop! Wait for me, sis!

00:15:56.630 --> 00:15:58.330
Siiiis!

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:04.790
Wanna prance around with me?

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:06.840
No thanks!

00:16:06.840 --> 00:16:08.360
Bummer...

00:16:13.880 --> 00:16:15.290
Where are we now?

00:16:15.290 --> 00:16:17.580
I feel like we may be lost.

00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:34.050
Welcome! We've got roasted chestnuts!

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:35.530
One bag, please!

00:16:35.530 --> 00:16:38.080
Comin' right up! Merry Christmas!

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:40.960
Santa...

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:44.470
Today was such a blast!

00:16:44.470 --> 00:16:47.020
Thanks for coming to get me, Chino!

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:50.460
So, you've been working at 
a roasted chestnut stand.

00:16:51.500 --> 00:16:53.130
It's staring to feel pretty cold.

00:16:53.580 --> 00:16:54.750
Here, have a chestnut!

00:16:59.380 --> 00:17:00.080
Ta-dah!

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:04.000
It's nice and warm!

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:07.210
You've gotten really good at that trick.

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:11.290
It's warm...

00:17:13.250 --> 00:17:17.080
You did say once before that 
you were envious of Santa.

00:17:17.710 --> 00:17:20.420
I suppose your dream
has come true now, to some extent.

00:17:21.960 --> 00:17:23.420
That's true!

00:17:24.690 --> 00:17:25.920
Is it raining?

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:30.040
I left the umbrella behind somewhere!

00:17:31.420 --> 00:17:33.420
That defeats the whole 
purpose of me coming...

00:17:35.290 --> 00:17:36.500
Wait, just look.

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:39.330
It's snowing!

00:18:13.580 --> 00:18:16.580
We can dance our way home
without any umbrella to carry!

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:19.750
Yahoo!

00:18:19.750 --> 00:18:23.100
Hearts are full~ Chests are full~!

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:25.330
Th-this is embarrassing!

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:27.500
Uh no, the chestnuts will spill!

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:32.380
I fell down...

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:33.540
And dragged me with you.

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:36.670
If anyone got dragged down, it was me!

00:18:40.750 --> 00:18:42.880
What do you suppose this line is for?

00:18:42.880 --> 00:18:45.290
Must be for some store that hit it big!

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:47.670
Has there always been a 
store like that nearby?

00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:49.540
Oh... it's our cafe!

00:18:50.130 --> 00:18:51.250
I don't believe it!

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:52.380
Impossible!

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:53.540
But it's your cafe!

00:18:56.630 --> 00:18:57.580
Welcome back!

00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:00.230
What's Rize's dad doing here?!

00:19:00.230 --> 00:19:03.700
Well, Takahiro's dear 
daughters, I'm the backup!

00:19:04.170 --> 00:19:07.750
Do you remember when Aoyama's editor
came to write a report on our cafe?

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:10.150
Yes, Miss Rin did.

00:19:10.150 --> 00:19:12.580
The magazine featuring 
that article went on sale.

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:16.590
The Heavenly Coffee
That A Family Inherited
From Their Grandfather

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:15.750
It provided us with some major publicity.

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:19.130
That's what inspired all 
these people to come?

00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:27.380
I... I'm happy, but it seems like we'll be
extra busy until the end of the year. Right, Cocoa?

00:19:29.080 --> 00:19:31.170
She's asleep?!

00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:32.380
Heavy...!

00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:38.750
My store... I have to work 
hard... and save up...

00:19:39.330 --> 00:19:42.360
Because I'm everyone's Santa...

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:45.210
Cocoa...

00:19:50.380 --> 00:19:51.330
Santa.

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:54.250
I finally became Santa!

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:56.000
I'm a sub for the theater club!

00:19:56.460 --> 00:19:57.750
Test prep!

00:19:58.380 --> 00:19:59.790
Studying!

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:02.010
Everyone's so busy.

00:20:02.380 --> 00:20:08.290
I, uh, I'm not much of a laborer,
but I think I can manage... p-probably.

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:11.830
No sweat! I'll deploy my squad
of tough and burly soldiers!

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:12.500
Huh?!

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:15.090
That would totally ruin the 
Christmas mood in here.

00:20:15.090 --> 00:20:16.380
Here, carry this for me.

00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:17.080
I'm on it!

00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:18.530
IT'S ALL OKAY!

00:20:18.530 --> 00:20:21.040
I'M GONNA WORK MY BUTT OFF!

00:20:21.040 --> 00:20:21.710
Huh?!

00:20:28.960 --> 00:20:31.960
She fell asleep right after 
getting into her uniform...

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:36.000
Well, she's been working nonstop since noon.

00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:41.830
She must be pretty cold wearing that.
I mean, it's still short-sleeved.

00:20:43.540 --> 00:20:48.250
Did you all forget to change back to
your winter uniforms from your new summer ones?

00:20:48.670 --> 00:20:52.750
You're right. The heater has been running
so it never really bothered me.

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:57.670
I've had my winter coat on for 
a while now! Fluff, fluff!

00:20:59.460 --> 00:21:01.830
Let's see. Where were the winter clothes?

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:13.790
Yellow and green uniforms...

00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:22.880
Oh? Cocoa went and completed
the other uniforms that were unfinished?

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:27.090
This size... I'm sure it would fit those two.

00:21:27.500 --> 00:21:28.880
Those two?

00:21:29.630 --> 00:21:32.460
Chino! Don't tell me you're calling in help
from our business rivals?!

00:21:32.920 --> 00:21:35.670
This season is busy beyond 
belief for everyone.

00:21:36.250 --> 00:21:36.980
But...!

00:21:45.210 --> 00:21:46.230
Chino?

00:21:46.230 --> 00:21:48.290
U-um, Chiya...

00:21:48.670 --> 00:21:51.250
Uh, I'd like to ask a 
favor of you and Syaro...

00:21:52.250 --> 00:21:53.960
It's a request for backup!

00:21:56.580 --> 00:21:58.440
We are friends forever!

00:21:58.440 --> 00:22:00.630
Friends! Okay! Friends!

00:22:00.630 --> 00:22:04.000
We'll make it happen! There's 
no problem since it's all okay!

00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:07.830
"There are mysterious things in this world"

00:22:07.830 --> 00:22:11.670
An inviting message from 
outside the familiar window

00:22:11.790 --> 00:22:15.540
Would you like to explore different places?

00:22:15.540 --> 00:22:19.250
Yeah, yeah, an adventure is 
needed every now and then

00:22:19.670 --> 00:22:23.380
And eventually on some street corner far away

00:22:23.540 --> 00:22:27.380
We'll get a craving to drink the usual coffee

00:22:27.380 --> 00:22:33.420
There are many things to realize 
if you just take a step back!

00:22:35.500 --> 00:22:37.080
Of course...

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:40.830
Right now being together is 
best, together forever is best

00:22:40.830 --> 00:22:44.630
Even amidst the changing seasons

00:22:44.630 --> 00:22:48.580
I want to keep these feelings, 
I want to treasure everyone

00:22:48.580 --> 00:22:52.540
I'm glad to have a place that I love

00:22:52.710 --> 00:22:56.420
Right now being together is best, 
that's right, together is best

00:22:56.420 --> 00:23:00.040
Even if you go somewhere 
else, be sure to come back

00:23:00.040 --> 00:23:04.170
I think that feeling is understood

00:23:04.170 --> 00:23:07.670
Because, after all, I got 
to see everyone today

00:23:07.920 --> 00:23:13.880
Seeing them whenever I want 
means... we're friends!

00:23:15.960 --> 00:23:17.710
We are friends forever!

00:23:17.960 --> 00:23:19.460
Friends! Okay! Friends!

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:23.580
We'll make it happen! There's 
no problem since it's okay!

00:23:26.460 --> 00:23:30.130
This year I'm Tippy Santa. 
That makes you my reindeer.

00:23:30.130 --> 00:23:30.920
Me?

00:23:31.250 --> 00:23:34.420
I'm not cut out to be the reindeer, 
you'd walk much faster.

00:23:32.790 --> 00:23:36.040
Bunnisode 11: The Cafe Of Smiles 
and the Rainbow Magician

00:23:34.420 --> 00:23:35.830
We're delivering gifts on foot?
